Sure.  There's no better way to persuade someone to listen than by
being hostile to them.  Great ambassadorship.

Again, this "lurk before talking" mandate I've been hearing for more
than 15 years is curiously Usenettish, and can't be reasonably
expected to be anticipated.  In most any informal, fun setting (as
talking about nethack surely should be) most people would jump right
in.  So it's stupid to verbally punish people for following the social
norm.

And this is all ignoring the significant fact, as I believe, that
people such as Raisse enjoy being rules-enforcer and berating other
people.


>... Your posts will be welcome if and when they are appropriate
